octoprint-tft (0.0~gitdbc3bc0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add missing x11-xserver-utils to Depends. disablescreenblank.sh calls
    xset, which that package provides; without it the ExecStartPost hook
    fails every start and systemd tears down the whole service in a loop
    (Restart=always + RestartSec=1s), even though Xorg and OctoPrint-TFT
    itself start and connect successfully every time -- the app's own
    logs look completely healthy, which is what made this easy to miss.
    Found by installing on a clean Trixie image with no desktop metapackages
    pulled in.

 -- darksid3r <darksid3r@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:47:54 +0000

octoprint-tft (0.0~gitdbc3bc0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Modernize build: replace dep (Gopkg.toml/Gopkg.lock) with Go modules.
  * Fix internal import path after forking (was still importing
    github.com/mcuadros/OctoPrint-TFT/ui, which pulled the stale upstream
    package instead of the local one).
  * Bump gotk3 off its 2019 master pin to v0.6.5 (commit e7a9e823, the fix
    for the "undefined: callback" build error in gdk/gdk_since_3_22.go);
    update ui/ call sites for the resulting API changes (glib.IdleAdd now
    returns one value, gtk.Dialog.Run() now returns gtk.ResponseType
    instead of int).
  * Pin sirupsen/logrus to v1.9.3 (later releases need Go 1.21 stdlib
    maps/slices, newer than Bookworm's golang-go).
  * Simplify debian/rules: drop the dh-golang/--buildsystem=golang
    pipeline and dh-systemd (gone from Bookworm, merged into debhelper)
    in favor of a plain `go build` override. Bump debhelper compat to 13.
  * Point Homepage/Vcs-*/debian/watch at the darksid3r fork.

 -- darksid3r <darksid3r@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

